 {"id": "DF-2026-7", "status": "pending", "priority": "P2", "title": "P2 — concurrent dogfood deliveries collide on the conventional scratch path and port and take each other's bunker agent: one lane's evidence tree was deleted, its daemon died on EADDRINUSE, and its install-leg agent was destroyed before collection", "acceptance_criteria": "Give the dogfood lane (and any other lane that writes a scratch tree under /tmp) a collision-proof scratch + port convention and an ownership marker for install agents. Deliver: (1) a documented, enforced rule that a lane's scratch root and TCP port are unique per RUN (tick label or random suffix), not per project+date — e.g. /tmp/<proj>-dogfood-<tick-label>-<rand>/ and a port drawn from a per-run random or lock file; (2) an install-leg ownership marker (agent id recorded in a per-run state file plus an ownership tag on the agent) so a `collect`/teardown can never destroy an agent a DIFFERENT lane spawned; (3) a pre-spawn deconfliction probe that fails loudly instead of silently continuing when the chosen scratch root already holds another lane's live state. Prove with a two-lane dry run on one host: lane A holds a scratch + agent, lane B starts, and lane B either picks a distinct path/port or aborts with the collision named — and lane A's evidence file is intact afterwards.", "acceptance": "Give the dogfood lane (and any other lane that writes a scratch tree under /tmp) a collision-proof scratch + port convention and an ownership marker for install agents. Deliver: (1) a documented, enforced rule that a lane's scratch root and TCP port are unique per RUN (tick label or random suffix), not per project+date — e.g. /tmp/<proj>-dogfood-<tick-label>-<rand>/ and a port drawn from a per-run random or lock file; (2) an install-leg ownership marker (agent id recorded in a per-run state file plus an ownership tag on the agent) so a `collect`/teardown can never destroy an agent a DIFFERENT lane spawned; (3) a pre-spawn deconfliction probe that fails loudly instead of silently continuing when the chosen scratch root already holds another lane's live state. Prove with a two-lane dry run on one host: lane A holds a scratch + agent, lane B starts, and lane B either picks a distinct path/port or aborts with the collision named — and lane A's evidence file is intact afterwards.", "reasoning": "Observed live during this tick (2026-10-27, duckbrain dogfood). (1) SCRATCH COLLISION: this lane created /tmp/df-dkb-1027/{root,evidence,logs} at 15:36 local; at ~15:40 the directory was replaced by ANOTHER Hermes session's duckbrain scratch (config.json with namespacesPath=/tmp/df-dkb-1027/namespaces, auth.json {apiKeys:[]}, home/, namespaces/), deleting this lane's evidence dir and its daemon's namespace root (the daemon then served 503 because its root was gone). The other session's daemon /proc environ shows HOME=/tmp/df-dkb-1027/own/home, PWD=/home/kara/duckbrain, HERMES_SESSION_CHAT_ID=b8f5c876-366a-4732-b540-05d8236dc5a5, and it left cli-remember.txt, cli-recall.txt, health-1..5.json, remember-help.txt, search-help.txt, status-help.txt, consolidate.txt, prod-health.json — a second dogfood-style delivery of the SAME project choosing the SAME date-based path convention (/tmp/df-dkb-<MMDD>). (2) PORT COLLISION: this lane's second daemon died at startup with `errno: -98, syscall: 'listen', address: '127.0.0.1', port: 3137` (daemon.log) because the other session had already bound 3137 with `node /home/kara/duckbrain/bin/duckbrain.js http --port=3137 --auth=none` (pid 11576, started 15:43:17 from the systemd --user manager); part of this lane's first confirmation pass was therefore answered by the OTHER session's daemon. (3) AGENT LOSS: this lane launched install agent 0908094c @ bunker-mvp at 20:40:31Z (battery began; cells repo-head/toolchain-bootstrap/fresh-install all OK). The other session captured that agent's evidence to /tmp/df-dkb-1027/install-agent-capture.txt at 15:45 and ran `bunker list --status all` a