-{"id": "DF-2026-12", "title": "P2 — CLI acceptance tests never exercise bin/duckbrain.js, so an untracked stale dist/ silently shadows the TypeScript source", "status": "pending", "priority": "P2", "complexity": 3, "acceptance_criteria": "bin/duckbrain.js prefers dist/bin/duckbrain.js when it exists, and dist/ is gitignored, so a host with an old build runs old code no matter what src/ says. Reproduced 2026-10-28: with the 2026-10-22 dist in place, `node bin/duckbrain.js status --namespace dogfood1027` printed 'Namespace: true / Path: ./memory/default' and exited 0 (the DF-2026-9 bug) while the merged src/ fix was present; after `npx tsc -p tsconfig.build.json` the same command answers correctly. Deliver: an end-to-end test that spawns bin/duckbrain.js (not an in-process import of src/cli/human.ts) covering the space-form and unknown-namespace arms, plus a CI step that builds the CLI before that test so the shipped entry point is what is verified. Prove the test fails against a deliberately stale dist and passes after a build.", "acceptance": "An E2E test spawns bin/duckbrain.js for the space-form/unknown-namespace arms, CI builds the CLI before running it, and the test fails when dist/ is deliberately stale.", "reasoning": "GitReins tier2 for DF-2026-9 (verdict c371acf6) marked the row INCOMPLETE because it ran the literal acceptance command in this repo and got the pre-fix behaviour. Root cause is not the patch: bin/duckbrain.js:16-19 prefers dist/, dist/ is gitignored (.gitignore:5) and stale (2026-10-22), and no CI step runs `pnpm build:cli` (grep of .github/workflows/ci.yml). src/cli/status-namespace-df2026-9.test.ts imports runHumanCLI in-process, so it can never see this class of regression.", "source": "foreman tick duckbrain-foreman-2026-10-28-02-09-38", "created_by": "foreman", "type": "test-gap", "created_at": "2026-10-27 21:46:59", "updated_at": "2026-10-27 21:46:59"}
