+{"id": "DF-2026-16", "title": "No L1 to L2 demotion: the injected memory file has been at 99% of its 20,000-char budget for weeks with no path to move an entry into DuckBrain", "status": "complete", "priority": "P1", "complexity": 3, "acceptance_criteria": "MEMORY.md measures 19,945 of 20,000 chars. The only way to add a fact today is to delete another one, because nothing demotes: there is no command that moves an entry from the file into a hermes-memory record and leaves a pointer behind. Deliver a demotion path modelled on the oh-my-hermes L1->L2 design: read the entry from the file itself (never from a paraphrase), refuse a partial entry, refuse redacted or oversized content (summary bound), write the record under hermes-memory with a content hash, then replace the file entry with a single pointer line [db#<sha12>] plus a one-line gloss. Dry run by default; every move journaled with reason and hash.", "reasoning": "This is the exact failure rlaope/oh-my-hermes documented (a pack that spills its cap silently loses the middle records while the receipt still counts them) and the same one we are living: a full file that forces deletion of durable rules to make room for new ones.", "source": null, "created_by": null, "type": null, "created_at": "2026-10-28 03:49:19", "updated_at": "2026-10-29 10:55:04", "detail": {"fingerprint": "5aaf2dd4af8a2be9cb10cf2fd390892f8e2732c1beba5c9c9decb4e2e07f5d25", "evidence": [{"run_id":"DF-2026-16-20261029","ts":"2026-10-29 10:55:04"}]}, "acceptance": "After one demotion pass the memory file is under 80% of budget, every demoted entry is retrievable byte-identically from hermes-memory, pointer lines resolve, and no entry was lost.", "foreman_note": "COPY PHASE DONE 2026-10-27: scripts/migrate_memory.py (4b7989a8) wrote 85 entries (MEMORY.md 66, USER.md 19) into hermes-memory as hashed records, idempotent, dry-run default; readback verified 85/85 by content match. CUT PHASE OPEN: nothing removed from the files yet (MEMORY.md still 19,945/20,000 chars) because demoting into a recall path that DF-2026-17 has not yet measured risks losing a rule silently. Next: record a recall baseline, then demote the oldest low-frequency entries to [db#sha] pointer lines and re-verify.\n\nRecovery closeout: branch rebased onto current main before serial merge; origin/main parity verified after subsequent push. ch:trace row=DF-2026-16 spec=.coding-hermes/board/tasks.jsonl#DF-2026-16 wave=.coding-hermes/waves/duckbrain-foreman-2026-10-29-08-57-58.json#workers[3] test=src/cli/memory-demote.test.ts doc=none evidence=github:run/40859204988 witness=origin:main@9edb4820 verdict=none:tier2-not-run commit=9edb4820 memory=none:write-after-board", "worker_status": "complete", "commit_hash": "9edb4820", "guard_result": "PASS", "ci_result": "RED", "worker_summary": "Recovered worker implementation: added dry-run-by-default L1 to L2 memory demotion CLI with validation, journal, and tests. Verified pnpm tsc --noEmit, focused demotion tests 4/4, and merged-tree full suite 241 files/2027 tests locally. CI on the containing main push failed only at pre-existing AGENTS.md GAP-012 count drift."}
 {"id": "DF-2026-17", "title": "Recall has no quality gate: text queries do not filter (q=cooldown returns 2 unrelated sync keys, q=zzzznothinglikethis returns 3) and no precision figure has ever been measured", "status": "pending", "priority": "P2", "complexity": 3, "acceptance_criteria": "Verified 2026-10-27 against the live API: GET /api/memories?namespace=coding-hermes&q=cooldown returned 2 records whose keys are /sync/coding-hermes/last-success and a scheduler-state note, while q=zzzznothinglikethis returned 3 records including /project/coding-hermes/board-census. A query with no possible match returns more rows than a real term, so any provider built on this endpoint would inject noise. No precision or recall number exists for the ledger anywhere. Deliver a fixed 20-case recall benchmark (query -> expected key or expected refusal), a runner that reports every rate with its denominator, and a scheduled run that fails loudly. Unanswered cases count as unanswered, never as correct.", "reasoning": "rlaope/oh-my-hermes treats routing and recall quality as measured objects with explicit denominators and 'unanswered is never correct'. Our ledger has none, so 'memory is working' is currently an impression rather than a number.", "source": null, "created_by": null, "type": null, "created_at": "2026-10-28 03:49:19", "updated_at": "2026-10-28 03:49:19", "detail": {"fingerprint": "486ac1fe4aaa14433c03c6fb8cec6b60805d3f09c718c815367edee02b5475a4"}, "acceptance": "A 20-case recall benchmark exists with a recorded baseline, runs on a schedule, fails non-zero below baseline, and every reported rate carries its denominator."}
 {"id": "DB-GAP-065", "title": "[P1] Namespace registry accumulates dead rows: 15,302 dir-missing mappings + 677 leaked auger-pytest dirs (1.1 GB) — add 'namespaces prune' and a drift guard", "status": "complete", "priority": "P1", "complexity": 3, "acceptance_criteria": "1. New `duckbrain namespaces prune` CLI verb (with a --dry-run default-to-safe mode) removes exactly those registry mappings whose resolved path does not exist, and prunes the matching namespaces/.s3state/<ns>.json manifest in the same pass; --dry-run prints the removed set and counts and mutates nothing.\n2. Idempotent and crash-safe: a second run removes 0 rows; the config is rewritten once via tmp+fsync+rename and the command aborts non-zero if the file changed between read and write (concurrent-writer guard).\n3. Never removes a mapping whose directory exists, and reuses the existing delete-namespace path-safety guard (resolved path must stay inside the namespaces root) so a mapping pointing outside the root is refused, not deleted.\n4. Tests: fixture config with live+dead rows mixed → prune removes exactly the dead set, leaves live rows byte-identical, prunes only those names' s3 manifests, and a second run is a no-op; out-of-root mapping is refused.\n5. Drift guard the fleet can act on: a check fails with an actionable message naming 'namespaces prune' when GET /api/namespaces reports directoryMissing above a threshold (>=25 rows, or dead rows > 2x live rows), so this can never accumulate silently again.\n6. Evidence recorded in the completion: before/after row count, payload bytes, and directoryMissing from GET /api/namespaces (2026-10-27 baseline 16,251 rows / 2,075,057 B / 15,299 missing → 276 rows / 24,343 B / 0).", "reasoning": "GET /api/namespaces unions the registry (duckbrain.config.json namespaceMappings) with the on-disk census. On 2026-10-27 the registry held 16,195 mappings of which 15,932 (98.4%) were auger pytest session namespaces and 15,296 pointed at directories that no longer existed; 677 leaked auger-pytest dirs still sat in namespaces/ (1.10 GB). Nothing prunes them: there is no prune verb, and deleteNamespace only clears a mapping when explicitly called. Result: 2,075,057-byte / 16,251-row listing at ~0.11 s with 16k existsSync calls per request, a 1.2 MB config rewritten in full on every namespace create/delete, and 176 stale .s3state manifests keeping ghost names on the 15-min push cadence. DB-GAP-060 fixed the STRAY namespaces/duckbrain.config.json; the ROOT registry is where the bulk accumulated, so the recurrence was never closed. 15,302 mappings and 677 dirs were pruned out-of-band on 2026-10-27 (backup + audit list at /home/kara/duckbrain-ns-prune-20261027; listing now 276 rows / 24,343 B, directoryMissing 0) — this row is the regression proof, not the cleanup.", "source": null, "created_by": null, "type": null, "created_at": "2026-10-28 03:49:27", "updated_at": "2026-10-28 04:55:00", "detail": {"fingerprint": "5fd70650f69f2de722b25a684ff7fcd8cc5458feb4e371f67c2838f58f3e2b20"}, "worktree": "/home/kara/worktrees/duckbrain-DB-GAP-065", "branch": "wt/DB-GAP-065", "commit_hash": "e36fe13d", "worker_status": "complete", "worker_summary": "Worker commit a203d3ca (wt/DB-GAP-065, recovered from dead tick duckbrain-foreman-2026-10-28-06-56-28) merged via 5cc4d3f3; evidence commit e36fe13d. Gates on merged tree: tsc --noEmit rc=0; vitest 237 suites / 1973 tests PASS (run twice: foreman + judge tier1); AGENTS.md count sync idempotent (237/1973). Live probes: namespaces prune dry-run -> 232 mappings, live 232, dead 0, refused 0, rc=0; GET /api/namespaces (scratch daemon :3999) -> 200, 279 rows, driftWarning correctly absent below threshold. Judge: first run INCOMPLETE on missing evidence artifact (2026-10-28/e9249a74), evidence closed in e36fe13d; re-judge verdict 2026-10-28/653c6cdc: tier2 COMPLETE (criterion PASS), overall FAIL only via the known repo-wide DF-2026-10 tier1 secrets condition (tracked .npmrc/.env.example credential-path class; gitleaks clean) — fix owned by pending row DF-2026-10. tier1 secrets: gitleaks clean; builtin 6 findings were .stryker-tmp sandbox residue (removed this tick). Fleet service duckbrain-http restarted on rebuilt dist/."}
 {"id": "DF-2026-18", "title": "Nothing turns chat sessions into durable records: the ledger only learns what cron syncs choose to write, so decisions made in conversation stay trapped in state.db", "status": "pending", "priority": "P2", "complexity": 3, "acceptance_criteria": "state.db holds every session (messages, tool calls, outcomes), but DuckBrain receives only what the per-project sync crons decide to write. A decision taken in a chat session therefore becomes durable only if a human or the agent hand-writes it \u2014 which is why 12 weeks of conversation produced a ledger full of sync markers and almost no decisions. Deliver a nightly distiller: for each session that ended in the last 24h, extract bounded, hash-keyed records (decisions, verified findings, open items) and write them under /session/<date>/<session-id>/<n>, skipping cron/system sessions, never storing transcripts, prompts or secrets, and deduping by message hash. Refuse a session whose transcript is unreadable rather than writing a summary of nothing.", "reasoning": "After two consecutive nightly runs the /session/ tree contains records for at least half the sessions that ended in that window; a rerun over unchanged input writes zero new records; every written record resolves to a session id that exists in state.db.", "source": null, "created_by": null, "type": null, "created_at": "2026-10-28 04:13:30", "updated_at": "2026-10-28 04:13:30", "detail": {"fingerprint": "8fb43bcfb233d3de5da97ca384e01941ade637a6b096f640f3eb1ac0c2c753f9"}, "acceptance": "Two nightly runs produce /session/ records for at least half the ended sessions, a rerun writes zero new records, and every record resolves to a real session id in state.db."}
 {"id":"DF-2026-19","title":"No measurement that the agent ever recalls: the twelve-week silent failure was invisible because nothing counted reads","status":"pending","priority":"P2","complexity":3,"acceptance_criteria":"Today's diagnosis found memory.provider empty since 2026-08-01 and no read-side metric anywhere: the namespace health check only asks whether a namespace answers and is non-empty, and the sync jobs only count writes. The provider added this evening can therefore run forever returning nothing and no surface would change colour. Deliver a read-side metric: a local counter written by the provider (prefetch calls, non-empty packs, distinct namespaces, records returned — the HTTP service cannot see MCP-side recall), a daily rollup series, and an alert or board row when a day has zero non-empty packs while the daemon is healthy. Report every rate with its denominator.","reasoning":"A 7-day series exists with per-day prefetch and non-empty-pack counts; a forced-empty day produces an alert; the rollup names the counter file path and the service health check it was compared against.","source":null,"created_by":null,"type":null,"created_at":"2026-10-28 04:13:30","updated_at":"2026-10-28 04:13:30","detail":{"fingerprint":"a9d59641089c0f7d599a5281adffc7f0a52566636a1335f1750d159e2612a626"},"acceptance":"A 7-day per-day series of prefetch and non-empty-pack counts exists, a forced-empty day raises an alert, and the rollup names the counter file plus the health check compared against it.","pm_note_2026_10_28":"PM input 2026-10-28: observed failure mode for the read-side metric to catch — provider token discovery falls back to the NEWEST-mtime ~/.duckbrain/*.token (no hermes/master token exists); a lane dropping a wrong-scope token would silently empty the pack. Same \"runs forever returning nothing\" class this row already targets."}
 {"id": "DB-GAP-66", "title": "No session receipt store: the ledger can hold facts but cannot answer 'was this skill even offered, and how much did this tick cost'", "status": "complete", "priority": "P2", "complexity": 3, "acceptance_criteria": "There is no bounded, queryable record of what happened inside a session interval: skill exposure and activation, tool calls and errors, model calls and errors, token counts, context peak, wall clock. Without it, 'the skill was not used' cannot be distinguished from 'nobody saw whether the skill was offered' - the open question behind SKILL-001 - and per-tick cost has to be reconstructed from state.db after the fact. Store session_activity_receipt-shaped records in their own namespace: closed key set, arrays capped, opaque refs only, NO prompts, transcripts, tool arguments, results or filesystem paths (rejected by key name and by shape). Every counter carries availability in observed/heuristic/unavailable and measurement in exact/floor, and a counter nobody observed is omitted or unavailable with a null value - never zero and never inferred from prose. Ingestion is idempotent on receipt_id: same id plus same observation records once, same id plus a different observation is quarantined. Every record carries its claim boundary in-band: not execution, verification, review or merge evidence. Expose a query that answers 'for skill X, how often was it exposed vs activated' and 'for session Y, the observed counters with their coverage'.", "reasoning": "Borrowed from rlaope/oh-my-hermes docs/SESSION-ACTIVITY-RECEIPTS.md (session_activity_receipt/v1) - the contract exists precisely so workflow learning, skill health and run-efficiency review reuse one observed record instead of each scraping a transcript. duckbrain is the store: it already has namespaces, keys, and an HTTP write/read surface, and it is where the fleet's durable facts already land. The strongest consumer is SKILL-001 (skill catalog and usage evidence) and DF-2026-19 (read-side counter), both of which currently have no honest data source. Three open rows in this repo touch provenance tangentially and none owns receipts (measured 2026-10-28).", "source": null, "created_by": null, "type": null, "created_at": "2026-10-28 13:50:18", "updated_at": "2026-10-29 02:49:59", "detail": {"fingerprint": "c42b988e5a443e88115c2077ec8b7436ec7987672b2b1113906a12a3746a8f50"}, "acceptance": "Receipts ingest idempotently by receipt_id; counters carry availability and measurement with unobserved values omitted or null, never zero; transcripts, tool args and paths are rejected by key and by shape; 'skill exposed vs activated' and 'session counters with coverage' queries return real data from a live ingest.", "worker_status": "complete", "foreman_note": "Dispatch wave duckbrain-foreman-2026-10-29-03-43-10; base origin/main @ 8426b628; worker model k3 @ kimi-for-coding.\n\nch:trace row=DB-GAP-66 spec=.coding-hermes/board/tasks.jsonl#DB-GAP-66 wave=.coding-hermes/waves/duckbrain-foreman-2026-10-29-03-43-10.json#worker-DB-GAP-66 test=src/receipts/sessionActivityReceipt.test.ts::48+src/http/routes/receipts-dbgap066.test.ts::HTTP doc=none prompt=/home/kara/.hermes/workspace/db-gap-66-brief.txt evidence=.gitreins/history/2026-10-29/bee86865/verdict.json witness=live:worker-tree-tests+tsc+HTTP-route-tests verdict=bee86865 commit=b3c940ea963e57730fe2cb025091192aa3577b45 memory=/project/duckbrain/status\n\nRECOVERY CLOSEOUT (tick duckbrain-foreman-2026-10-29-06-45-22): recovered wave duckbrain-foreman-2026-10-29-03-43-10. Worker commits 220f07ca + b3c940ea were merged (91058e82) on the foreman branch; this tick landed them on canonical main: local main fast-forwarded 8426b628..ee42f2ea and pushed to origin + ghgitlab mirror (parity 0 on both). STALE-BASE check PASS (merge-base == origin/main == recorded base 8426b628). Board-mixing check PASS (true-base diff touches 0 board paths; only AGENTS.md + 5 src files). Gates on the merged tree: focused receipts tests 4